WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.447
You type delulu, job, interview.

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:06.425
A result title says only Job interview

00:00:06.445 --> 00:00:09.311
expectations. Where did delulu go?

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.167
It is tempting to tell a story about a

00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:12.713
clever semantic engine.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:15.613
But the same screen can fit several very

00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:16.888
different histories.

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:21.100
Follow four possible routes.

00:00:21.275 --> 00:00:23.639
Each is a mechanism the chapter asks us to

00:00:23.659 --> 00:00:26.809
check, not a diagnosis of a named product.

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:29.039
Several routes could operate in the same

00:00:29.059 --> 00:00:29.889
search.

00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:33.844
First, a word can disappear during routine

00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:36.549
analysis. In the chapter's illustration,

00:00:36.737 --> 00:00:38.315
you type the job interview.

00:00:38.464 --> 00:00:41.343
An optional stop-word rule removes the.

00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:43.727
Retrieval receives job interview.

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:46.279
The discarded word was never a condition

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:47.181
at lookup.

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.982
This example depends on the analyser.

00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:52.367
It does not say every system removes the

00:00:52.387 --> 00:00:56.348
same words. Tokenisation, normalisation,

00:00:56.369 --> 00:00:58.604
stemming and stop-word handling prepare

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.962
strings for matching; none by itself

00:01:00.982 --> 00:01:03.230
establishes understanding of meaning.

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:06.915
Second, an upstream rewrite can change

00:01:06.935 --> 00:01:08.538
what retrieval receives.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.257
You type delulu job expectations.

00:01:11.394 --> 00:01:13.732
A transformation replaces delulu with

00:01:13.752 --> 00:01:16.271
unrealistic. Retrieval then looks for

00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:19.492
unrealistic job expectations.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:22.057
The original word need not appear in a

00:01:22.077 --> 00:01:23.177
matching record.

00:01:23.746 --> 00:01:26.235
Unlike routine analysis, this is an

00:01:26.255 --> 00:01:28.206
explicit reformulation.

00:01:28.382 --> 00:01:30.836
The illustration is not evidence that a

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:33.451
particular product made this rewrite.

00:01:33.613 --> 00:01:36.609
To establish that, inspect the processed

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.070
query or obtain documentation about that

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:39.933
stage.

00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:43.367
Third, delulu can remain in the retrieval

00:01:43.387 --> 00:01:45.712
input without being required.

00:01:45.874 --> 00:01:48.007
An any-match rule admits a record

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.145
containing job and interview.

00:01:50.307 --> 00:01:53.328
A delulu match could add scoring evidence,

00:01:53.452 --> 00:01:55.687
but its absence need not exclude the

00:01:55.707 --> 00:01:56.395
record.

00:01:56.954 --> 00:01:59.011
An optional term might even have no

00:01:59.031 --> 00:02:01.626
posting list anywhere in the index.

00:02:01.763 --> 00:02:03.843
Other terms can still admit records.

00:02:03.992 --> 00:02:06.421
Make that unmatched term compulsory under

00:02:06.441 --> 00:02:10.518
strict AND, and the eligible set is empty.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.224
The difference is the execution rule.

00:02:14.139 --> 00:02:16.606
Fourth, the term may have matched evidence

00:02:16.626 --> 00:02:18.861
you cannot see in the excerpt.

00:02:19.036 --> 00:02:21.838
The visible title says Job interview

00:02:21.858 --> 00:02:25.485
expectations. The indexed abstract says,

00:02:25.505 --> 00:02:28.088
We examine delulu expectations.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.511
A lexical match occurred, but the title

00:02:30.531 --> 00:02:31.941
did not display it.

00:02:32.494 --> 00:02:35.334
Other indexed fields, expanded terms,

00:02:35.535 --> 00:02:37.976
older indexed versions or off-page

00:02:37.996 --> 00:02:39.870
evidence may also matter.

00:02:40.006 --> 00:02:42.370
Inspect the searchable fields and the

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.064
indexed representation before concluding

00:02:45.084 --> 00:02:47.164
that no lexical match happened.

00:02:47.339 --> 00:02:49.780
A snippet is only a small window.

00:02:50.687 --> 00:02:52.314
Keep four jobs distinct.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.789
Analysis prepares strings.

00:02:54.964 --> 00:02:57.495
Execution rules decide which clauses are

00:02:57.515 --> 00:03:00.704
required, optional or subject to a minimum

00:03:00.724 --> 00:03:03.307
match. Query understanding interprets

00:03:03.327 --> 00:03:06.774
things such as entities, dates, phrases or

00:03:06.794 --> 00:03:09.299
intent. Transformation changes what

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:10.845
retrieval receives.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.712
Understanding can inform a decision while

00:03:13.732 --> 00:03:16.314
leaving every word unchanged.

00:03:16.477 --> 00:03:19.137
It becomes relevant to a missing word when

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:21.559
its interpretation causes a change.

00:03:21.708 --> 00:03:24.562
Understanding alone is not a fifth history

00:03:24.582 --> 00:03:26.598
that magically removes a term.

00:03:27.519 --> 00:03:30.071
A question in natural language can pass

00:03:30.091 --> 00:03:32.326
through a parser or language model that

00:03:32.346 --> 00:03:34.593
constructs a Boolean expression.

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:37.017
The lexical engine can then apply Boolean

00:03:37.037 --> 00:03:39.980
admission and BM twenty-five ranking over

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.294
an inverted index.

00:03:41.837 --> 00:03:44.258
The form of the input does not identify

00:03:44.278 --> 00:03:45.546
the retrieval method.

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:48.601
To bridge a vocabulary gap, one route

00:03:48.621 --> 00:03:50.779
changes the query and keeps lexical

00:03:50.799 --> 00:03:52.467
matching. Another changes the

00:03:52.487 --> 00:03:54.993
representation so related texts can be

00:03:55.013 --> 00:03:58.549
retrieved without shared analysed terms.

00:03:59.444 --> 00:04:01.888
Return to the title without delulu.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.775
Was the word removed in analysis, changed

00:04:04.795 --> 00:04:07.907
in a rewrite, retained as optional, or

00:04:07.927 --> 00:04:09.929
matched outside the excerpt?

00:04:10.117 --> 00:04:12.764
The title alone cannot choose among them.

00:04:12.939 --> 00:04:15.239
A product name and a result count cannot

00:04:15.259 --> 00:04:16.347
settle it either.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.113
Ask for the processed query, the admission

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:22.026
rules, the indexed fields and evidence

00:04:22.046 --> 00:04:23.726
about the retrieval pipeline.

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:25.995
Part One separates lexical search from

00:04:26.015 --> 00:04:28.404
strict all-term Boolean search.

00:04:28.579 --> 00:04:30.144
The next chapters investigate

00:04:30.164 --> 00:04:32.670
representations, while keeping the rest of

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.229
the pipeline in view.
